WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.318 --> 00:00:01.370
- If you don't fight,

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:05.276
go after with such tenacity
your goals in life,

00:00:05.276 --> 00:00:07.605
what are you leaving a significant other

00:00:07.605 --> 00:00:09.050
to admire about you?

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.879
If you hang out with
somebody with a dark cloud,

00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:12.970
the rain going to get you eventually.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.020
So you go over there somewhere
with your little dark cloud,

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.248
'cause I like the sun.

00:00:17.248 --> 00:00:19.695
I didn't hear the naysayers
when they were like,

00:00:19.695 --> 00:00:21.277
you're too old to go to California.

00:00:21.277 --> 00:00:22.481
If you don't hit by 25,

00:00:22.481 --> 00:00:24.546
you're not going to make it.

00:00:24.546 --> 00:00:25.851
I will be 46 this year.

00:00:25.851 --> 00:00:27.816
I am just touching the surface.

00:00:27.816 --> 00:00:29.368
- She began her Hollywood career

00:00:29.368 --> 00:00:31.703
in several guest roles on TV shows

00:00:31.703 --> 00:00:34.724
before making her big
breakthrough in Baby Boy.

00:00:34.724 --> 00:00:36.363
She's won a Golden Globe Award

00:00:36.363 --> 00:00:38.432
and has been nominated
for two Emmy Awards.

00:00:38.432 --> 00:00:41.821
She also released a New York
Times bestselling autobiography

00:00:41.821 --> 00:00:43.724
titled Around the Way Girl.

00:00:43.724 --> 00:00:45.105
She's Taraji P. Henson,

00:00:45.105 --> 00:00:47.878
and here's my take on her
top 10 rules for success.

00:00:47.878 --> 00:00:49.556
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:49.556 --> 00:00:51.717
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:52.791
Also guys, as you're watching,

00:00:52.791 --> 00:00:54.871
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:54.871 --> 00:00:56.514
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:56.514 --> 00:00:59.072
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:59.072 --> 00:01:00.455
Also, when you write it down,

00:01:00.455 --> 00:01:03.528
it's much more likely to
lock in for yourself as well.

00:01:03.528 --> 00:01:04.361
Enjoy.

00:01:07.643 --> 00:01:11.476
(triumphant orchestral music)

00:01:17.591 --> 00:01:19.525
- [Reporter] What's the
biggest risk you've taken

00:01:19.525 --> 00:01:21.775
that you feel has paid off?

00:01:22.677 --> 00:01:26.625
- The biggest risk I've
taken that has paid off,

00:01:26.625 --> 00:01:28.834
I might have to say Cookie.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:33.001
I mean, I was very nervous
when I received the script.

00:01:34.856 --> 00:01:36.852
She wasn't the most likable character,

00:01:36.852 --> 00:01:38.659
and I've played some
pretty edgy characters,

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:41.634
but this one was particularly a challenge

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.422
because it was primetime
network television,

00:01:44.422 --> 00:01:47.799
and I wasn't sure how
people would receive her.

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:50.092
I mean, she beat her son with a broom,

00:01:50.092 --> 00:01:51.469
even though he deserved it.

00:01:51.469 --> 00:01:53.527
(audience chuckling)

00:01:53.527 --> 00:01:55.120
She called one son a faggot.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.287
I mean, erm, it was scary,

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:01.357
but I'm the type of artist

00:02:01.357 --> 00:02:03.282
that if the role doesn't scare me,

00:02:03.282 --> 00:02:05.142
I don't want it, 'cause it's not

00:02:05.142 --> 00:02:07.564
going to change me as a person.

00:02:07.564 --> 00:02:08.981
So I took a risk,

00:02:10.781 --> 00:02:11.931
and that's what you do as artists.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:15.525
You jump in feet first
and you see where it goes,

00:02:15.525 --> 00:02:18.757
and I knew that we had something special.

00:02:18.757 --> 00:02:22.771
I don't just jump feet
first for any project.

00:02:22.771 --> 00:02:24.583
I knew this was something special.

00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:27.080
I knew that what Fox was trying to do,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.619
what Lee Daniels and Danny Strong

00:02:28.619 --> 00:02:30.913
were trying to do and
what I was trying to do

00:02:30.913 --> 00:02:32.392
was shake up television.

00:02:32.392 --> 00:02:33.664
It's too safe.

00:02:33.664 --> 00:02:36.042
You know, life is not safe,

00:02:36.042 --> 00:02:39.205
and I think we did that with this show.

00:02:39.205 --> 00:02:42.590
So I'm so proud to be
a part of this project

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:45.398
and I'm so proud that Fox
believed in us and took a chance,

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.509
'cause that's what art is about, isn't it?

00:02:47.509 --> 00:02:49.523
Taking chances, taking risks.

00:02:49.523 --> 00:02:51.008
(laughing)

00:02:51.008 --> 00:02:53.173
I'm graduated college
and I have, you know,

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.762
this degree in fine arts,

00:02:54.762 --> 00:02:57.313
and my dad saw me coming
and going to work every day,

00:02:57.313 --> 00:02:59.432
and he was like, what are you doing?

00:02:59.432 --> 00:03:00.649
And I was like, making a living.

00:03:00.649 --> 00:03:01.764
What are you talking about?

00:03:01.764 --> 00:03:03.488
And I was in a transitional period,

00:03:03.488 --> 00:03:05.150
because my son's father and I,

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.940
we had just broken up
and I had this degree

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:10.529
and I was just living.

00:03:10.529 --> 00:03:12.268
And my dad saw it and he was like,

00:03:12.268 --> 00:03:14.322
"How do you expect to
catch fish on dry land?"

00:03:14.322 --> 00:03:15.244
And I was like, what are you,

00:03:15.244 --> 00:03:17.048
he always spoke in metaphors.

00:03:17.048 --> 00:03:18.029
(audience laughing)

00:03:18.029 --> 00:03:19.723
I was like, can you just
speak plain English?

00:03:19.723 --> 00:03:22.307
He was like, "How are you
going to get acting jobs

00:03:22.307 --> 00:03:23.283
"when they're not here?

00:03:23.283 --> 00:03:26.121
"You need to go to LA where the jobs are."

00:03:26.121 --> 00:03:28.444
So my family threw a party.

00:03:28.444 --> 00:03:29.335
We were broke.

00:03:29.335 --> 00:03:31.702
They raised $700 and I moved to LA,

00:03:31.702 --> 00:03:33.415
and I took my son and my dad,

00:03:33.415 --> 00:03:34.609
may he rest in peace,

00:03:34.609 --> 00:03:37.622
he was like, maybe you
should leave Marcell here.

00:03:37.622 --> 00:03:39.451
And I was like, I'm not leaving my son.

00:03:39.451 --> 00:03:40.546
- Yeah.
- That's my kid.

00:03:40.546 --> 00:03:42.412
Then I got out and freaked
out and I was like,

00:03:42.412 --> 00:03:43.513
maybe I should send him back.

00:03:43.513 --> 00:03:45.862
And my dad was like, no,
that's your blessing.

00:03:45.862 --> 00:03:46.695
He's your blessing.

00:03:46.695 --> 00:03:47.828
He's going to keep you focused.

00:03:47.828 --> 00:03:49.296
You were right, your instinct was right.

00:03:49.296 --> 00:03:50.767
You should've taken him.

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:53.184
So $700 and my son is now 21.

00:03:54.436 --> 00:03:55.933
He's in school now.

00:03:55.933 --> 00:03:57.545
- Look at you.
- He's studying to be,

00:03:57.545 --> 00:03:59.408
right, and look at me.

00:03:59.408 --> 00:04:00.697
- Tell us about how while you were

00:04:00.697 --> 00:04:02.274
in the movie Benjamin Button.

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:04.057
- Yeah, I don't want people to get upset.

00:04:04.057 --> 00:04:05.966
It's not that I expected to be paid

00:04:05.966 --> 00:04:08.351
as much as Brad Pitt or Cate Blanchett.

00:04:08.351 --> 00:04:10.212
I understand, I'm just,

00:04:10.212 --> 00:04:11.908
I'm new to the game.
- Yeah.

00:04:11.908 --> 00:04:14.374
- But what we were asking for didn't seem

00:04:14.374 --> 00:04:16.662
like an astronomical amount,

00:04:16.662 --> 00:04:17.495
you know what I mean?

00:04:17.495 --> 00:04:21.723
It was fair for me where I
was that time in my career.

00:04:21.723 --> 00:04:23.651
And they didn't come back with that.

00:04:23.651 --> 00:04:25.708
- They didn't.
- We were heartbroken.

00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:28.180
But see, that's when you
have to check your ego,

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.798
'cause if I had let ego
take control of that,

00:04:30.798 --> 00:04:32.409
I wouldn't have taken the job

00:04:32.409 --> 00:04:33.960
and I would've missed my moment.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.476
So I had to set pride aside--

00:04:35.476 --> 00:04:37.067
- Suck it up--
- Suck it up,

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.211
and I had to bite my tongue a lot,

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:42.248
and I just had to stay
focused on the bigger picture.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.447
- But that's smart business.

00:04:43.447 --> 00:04:44.280
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.899
- Do you ever get nervous anymore?

00:04:45.899 --> 00:04:46.732
- Absolutely.

00:04:46.732 --> 00:04:47.927
- You do?
- I'm human.

00:04:47.927 --> 00:04:49.287
Absolutely.

00:04:49.287 --> 00:04:50.451
- You look like you just,

00:04:50.451 --> 00:04:52.701
you go up there and
you're not even worried.

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:55.537
- Well, there's a moment where
there's a fear that arises,

00:04:55.537 --> 00:04:57.262
and I check it.

00:04:57.262 --> 00:04:58.212
It's not that I ignore it.

00:04:58.212 --> 00:05:00.939
I go, okay, that's fear, and--

00:05:00.939 --> 00:05:01.772
- Okay.
- You know,

00:05:01.772 --> 00:05:03.949
I'm a faith-based person
and that's everything.

00:05:03.949 --> 00:05:05.939
I live in faith--
- High five, high five.

00:05:05.939 --> 00:05:07.969
- Yeah, so, faith and fear can't--

00:05:07.969 --> 00:05:10.035
- Yeah.
- They can't live--

00:05:10.035 --> 00:05:10.932
- [Both] Together.

00:05:10.932 --> 00:05:14.040
- So when it comes up, you know,

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.029
I just check it.

00:05:15.029 --> 00:05:16.870
I go, oh okay, I recognize that--

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:18.369
- Got it.
- But that's not where I live.

00:05:18.369 --> 00:05:19.492
- You're not going to live by it.
- Right.

00:05:19.492 --> 00:05:20.825
- Fear is not an option.

00:05:20.825 --> 00:05:22.009
- And that's what nervousness is.

00:05:22.009 --> 00:05:23.272
That's what that energy is.

00:05:23.272 --> 00:05:25.989
It's that moment to choose
to give into that nerve

00:05:25.989 --> 00:05:28.049
or to rise above, you know,

00:05:28.049 --> 00:05:30.673
so we battle that every day as humans.

00:05:30.673 --> 00:05:31.506
I am human.

00:05:31.506 --> 00:05:32.890
I'm not a robot.

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.190
- I love that you realized
that that's a choice.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.023
- Yeah.

00:05:36.023 --> 00:05:37.448
- Because everybody kept asking me,

00:05:37.448 --> 00:05:38.281
what does it feel like,

00:05:38.281 --> 00:05:39.769
what does it feel like?

00:05:39.769 --> 00:05:41.103
When you go the nomination,

00:05:41.103 --> 00:05:43.173
that little girl from Washington, D.C.,

00:05:43.173 --> 00:05:46.194
what did it feel like
when you heard your name?

00:05:46.194 --> 00:05:47.502
- Mine was a rollercoaster ride.

00:05:47.502 --> 00:05:50.244
I was nominated for this
and wasn't for that.

00:05:50.244 --> 00:05:52.051
You know, so I really
put it out of my head,

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:56.107
'cause I don't really do
what I do for the awards.

00:05:56.107 --> 00:05:56.955
You know, like you said,

00:05:56.955 --> 00:05:59.089
if you're passionate about your work,

00:05:59.089 --> 00:06:00.788
all of the accolades will come.

00:06:00.788 --> 00:06:02.322
- That's right.
- You got to stay focused

00:06:02.322 --> 00:06:04.768
on what God put you on earth to do.

00:06:04.768 --> 00:06:07.472
- Right.
- So that's number one.

00:06:07.472 --> 00:06:09.972
I finally get to LA, graduate.

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.671
I have a kid in college.

00:06:14.521 --> 00:06:17.021
And I have to pursue my dream,

00:06:19.962 --> 00:06:21.306
because if I don't,

00:06:21.306 --> 00:06:22.982
what am I teaching my son?

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.880
So I moved to California with $700

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.213
in my pocket and my toddler.

00:06:28.515 --> 00:06:31.432
And I have to fight the good fight,

00:06:32.714 --> 00:06:34.513
because people are telling me I can't.

00:06:34.513 --> 00:06:35.720
You can't do this, you can't.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:37.106
Are you crazy?

00:06:37.106 --> 00:06:38.521
You're moving to California with your son?

00:06:38.521 --> 00:06:39.724
You'll never make it.

00:06:39.724 --> 00:06:42.369
I was 26 when I decided to come here.

00:06:42.369 --> 00:06:43.433
There's the age thing.

00:06:43.433 --> 00:06:45.574
Oh, you're too old.

00:06:45.574 --> 00:06:48.105
If you listen to people,

00:06:48.105 --> 00:06:50.091
(audience laughing)

00:06:50.091 --> 00:06:54.925
and if you allow people to
project their fears onto you,

00:06:54.925 --> 00:06:56.802
you won't live.

00:06:56.802 --> 00:06:59.084
What if I believed those people

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:01.477
who told me that when I became pregnant

00:07:01.477 --> 00:07:03.492
in college that I wouldn't finish?

00:07:03.492 --> 00:07:06.424
I walked across that stage
with my son on my hip

00:07:06.424 --> 00:07:09.182
and I collected my degree, my diploma.

00:07:09.182 --> 00:07:11.853
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:07:11.853 --> 00:07:14.363
I didn't hear the naysayers
when they were like,

00:07:14.363 --> 00:07:15.897
you're too old to go to California.

00:07:15.897 --> 00:07:17.063
If you don't hit by 25,

00:07:17.063 --> 00:07:19.234
you're not going to make it.

00:07:19.234 --> 00:07:20.469
I will be 46 this year.

00:07:20.469 --> 00:07:22.125
I am just touching the surface.

00:07:22.125 --> 00:07:24.285
I am just getting started.

00:07:24.285 --> 00:07:26.952
Everything in life that's coming to you

00:07:26.952 --> 00:07:28.227
is going to come through you.

00:07:28.227 --> 00:07:29.875
It starts inside of you.

00:07:29.875 --> 00:07:32.800
You know, whether it's love from another,

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.063
from a male, from whoever.

00:07:35.063 --> 00:07:37.134
That love has to start within you.

00:07:37.134 --> 00:07:39.614
If you don't know how
to take care of yourself

00:07:39.614 --> 00:07:42.317
or care for yourself first, you know,

00:07:42.317 --> 00:07:45.342
how are you going to
teach someone else to?

00:07:45.342 --> 00:07:47.434
You know, if you don't fight,

00:07:47.434 --> 00:07:51.361
go after with such tenacity
your goals in life,

00:07:51.361 --> 00:07:53.641
what are you leaving a significant other

00:07:53.641 --> 00:07:55.161
to admire about you?

00:07:55.161 --> 00:07:57.355
It all starts with you, you know.

00:07:57.355 --> 00:07:59.340
You're the temple and you have control.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:00.763
You're in a bad situation?

00:08:00.763 --> 00:08:02.401
It's up to you to get out of it.

00:08:02.401 --> 00:08:04.445
You can't give another human

00:08:04.445 --> 00:08:06.906
the responsibility of your happiness.

00:08:06.906 --> 00:08:09.867
You know, my father
told me a long time ago,

00:08:09.867 --> 00:08:11.784
he said, "Life is choice-driven,"

00:08:11.784 --> 00:08:15.438
and we're talking about a man
who had a very rocky past.

00:08:15.438 --> 00:08:18.002
And you know, once he
had his epiphany in life,

00:08:18.002 --> 00:08:20.751
when he gave his life
to Christ and, you know,

00:08:20.751 --> 00:08:25.447
he started seeing life in
a more optimistic lens,

00:08:25.447 --> 00:08:27.349
and that's when he hit me with it.

00:08:27.349 --> 00:08:29.152
"Taraji, you know, life is choice-driven.

00:08:29.152 --> 00:08:30.757
"I made some bad choices in life,

00:08:30.757 --> 00:08:32.514
"but that doesn't mean I can't change,

00:08:32.514 --> 00:08:36.811
"I can't change my mind to make
better choices for myself."

00:08:36.811 --> 00:08:39.318
So that's something that I live by.

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:40.339
You got to have fun.

00:08:40.339 --> 00:08:42.138
You got to laugh to keep from crying,

00:08:42.138 --> 00:08:43.767
'cause there's a lot
going on in this world.

00:08:43.767 --> 00:08:45.996
And I really like to laugh a lot.

00:08:45.996 --> 00:08:47.136
And I think, you know,

00:08:47.136 --> 00:08:47.969
people are like, you look so young.

00:08:47.969 --> 00:08:49.170
I laugh a lot.
- Right.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.146
- I laugh at myself.

00:08:50.146 --> 00:08:52.179
I don't take myself too seriously.

00:08:52.179 --> 00:08:55.645
And like I said, I surround
myself with good energy,

00:08:55.645 --> 00:08:57.379
'cause energy is transferrable.

00:08:57.379 --> 00:08:59.442
If you hang out with
somebody with a dark cloud,

00:08:59.442 --> 00:09:01.418
the rain going to get you eventually.

00:09:01.418 --> 00:09:04.343
So you go over there somewhere
with your little dark cloud,

00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:05.789
'cause I like the sun.

00:09:05.789 --> 00:09:06.931
I usually don't turn,

00:09:06.931 --> 00:09:08.721
I don't run from things that scare me.

00:09:08.721 --> 00:09:10.654
That usually means I should do it.

00:09:10.654 --> 00:09:12.479
- Yeah.
- If I feel too confident,

00:09:12.479 --> 00:09:13.951
it's like I could do
this with my eyes closed,

00:09:13.951 --> 00:09:15.714
then I'm not servicing my fans,

00:09:15.714 --> 00:09:18.198
the script, the project, or the character.

00:09:18.198 --> 00:09:19.031
Why do it?

00:09:19.031 --> 00:09:22.294
Somebody else out there more
hungry might bless it better.

00:09:22.294 --> 00:09:24.831
You know, so I, yeah,

00:09:24.831 --> 00:09:26.077
I love challenges.

00:09:26.077 --> 00:09:30.343
What I love about art is
you have to take risks,

00:09:30.343 --> 00:09:33.504
and that's the work that sticks out,

00:09:33.504 --> 00:09:35.320
the stuff that's not so safe.

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:38.667
I sang about pimps and
whores at the Oscars.

00:09:38.667 --> 00:09:39.500
I did.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.814
I sang It's Hard Out Here for a Pimp.

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:42.934
Yeah, they won.

00:09:42.934 --> 00:09:44.271
My manager calls and he's like,

00:09:44.271 --> 00:09:45.421
"I have this script,"

00:09:45.421 --> 00:09:46.566
you know, and I was like, what is it?

00:09:46.566 --> 00:09:47.536
And he's like, "It's a pilot."

00:09:47.536 --> 00:09:48.833
I was like, for TV?

00:09:48.833 --> 00:09:50.789
Didn't I tell you I'm done with TV?

00:09:50.789 --> 00:09:51.664
So he's like, "Read it."

00:09:51.664 --> 00:09:53.352
I read it, I'm like, this is stupid.

00:09:53.352 --> 00:09:54.685
Ugh, hip-hop.

00:09:54.685 --> 00:09:56.942
Dumb, dumb, du-dumb-dumb.

00:09:56.942 --> 00:10:00.793
Ooh, ooh, oh my God, oh my God, oh my God.

00:10:00.793 --> 00:10:02.647
And then that fear thing comes up,

00:10:02.647 --> 00:10:03.728
and it's like, okay,

00:10:03.728 --> 00:10:05.082
well, clearly this is a challenge.

00:10:05.082 --> 00:10:05.915
Oh my God, Cookie.

00:10:05.915 --> 00:10:07.300
We're going to piss so many people off.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:09.085
And then once I wrapped my mind around

00:10:09.085 --> 00:10:11.845
how to deal with Cookie, tell her truth,

00:10:11.845 --> 00:10:14.459
you know, tell the why she's this woman,

00:10:14.459 --> 00:10:16.193
why she hit her son with the broom,

00:10:16.193 --> 00:10:17.268
if you stick to the truth,

00:10:17.268 --> 00:10:18.264
people will love her.

00:10:18.264 --> 00:10:21.667
They set up a Skype session with Lee.

00:10:21.667 --> 00:10:22.698
Well, yeah, I knew Lee,

00:10:22.698 --> 00:10:24.985
but I had never worked with Lee.

00:10:24.985 --> 00:10:26.806
Because, you know, the last time we met

00:10:26.806 --> 00:10:29.347
was in the audition for Precious,

00:10:29.347 --> 00:10:30.507
and he wanted me for the teacher,

00:10:30.507 --> 00:10:32.322
and I was like, well, I
want to play Precious.

00:10:32.322 --> 00:10:34.116
That's the role, I mean.

00:10:34.116 --> 00:10:35.302
He thought I was crazy.

00:10:35.302 --> 00:10:36.218
But I was like, look,

00:10:36.218 --> 00:10:38.951
you turned Charlize Theron into a monster.

00:10:38.951 --> 00:10:40.210
But yeah, so that was the last time

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:42.967
I saw him on a job, you
know, potential job,

00:10:42.967 --> 00:10:45.469
so he probably still was thinking,

00:10:45.469 --> 00:10:47.250
oh, this bitch is crazy.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.921
I don't even know if I should call her.

00:10:48.921 --> 00:10:50.883
But so he's in Japan,

00:10:50.883 --> 00:10:53.216
and we have a Skype session,

00:10:53.216 --> 00:10:54.876
and you know, I'm not tripping.

00:10:54.876 --> 00:10:55.709
I don't care.

00:10:55.709 --> 00:10:56.680
I don't have to go back to TV.

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:58.092
I'm waiting for my big movie.

00:10:58.092 --> 00:10:59.262
(laughing)

00:10:59.262 --> 00:11:02.022
Spielberg is going to
call me for sure, I know.

00:11:02.022 --> 00:11:04.899
I say to him, I really like this script.

00:11:04.899 --> 00:11:05.955
I think it's amazing.

00:11:05.955 --> 00:11:07.128
I think it's game-changing.

00:11:07.128 --> 00:11:08.105
I think, you know,

00:11:08.105 --> 00:11:09.820
if I can't do it with Terrence,

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:11.210
I'm not interested.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:12.989
I didn't even have the job.

00:11:12.989 --> 00:11:13.980
End of the Skype session,

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.077
he was like, this bitch just Cookied me.

00:11:16.077 --> 00:11:17.192
(laughing)

00:11:17.192 --> 00:11:18.645
Cookie is the American dream.

00:11:18.645 --> 00:11:21.785
She started from nothing
and now she's at the top.

00:11:21.785 --> 00:11:23.431
Started from the bottom, now we here.

00:11:23.431 --> 00:11:24.806
I mean, that's like,

00:11:24.806 --> 00:11:26.863
I'm the American dream.

00:11:26.863 --> 00:11:31.772
I wasn't born with a silver
spoon in my mouth, you know.

00:11:31.772 --> 00:11:32.820
I had a passion.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:35.153
I had a dream and I dived in

00:11:36.378 --> 00:11:39.628
and I went for my dream, and here I am.

00:11:41.684 --> 00:11:43.123
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:11:43.123 --> 00:11:45.860
I made this video because
Alea Turner asked me to.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:46.936
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:11:46.936 --> 00:11:48.629
that you want me to profile next,

00:11:48.629 --> 00:11:49.688
leave it down in the comments below

00:11:49.688 --> 00:11:50.926
and I'll see what I can do.

00:11:50.926 --> 00:11:52.182
I'd also love to know which of the clips

00:11:52.182 --> 00:11:54.234
that you heard today had
the biggest impact on you.

00:11:54.234 --> 00:11:55.997
What lesson are you
going to take from this

00:11:55.997 --> 00:11:58.406
and immediately apply to
your life or your business?

00:11:58.406 --> 00:11:59.455
Leave it in the comments below

00:11:59.455 --> 00:12:01.165
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:12:01.165 --> 00:12:03.258
Finally, I want to give a
quick shout-out to Celia Lopez.

00:12:03.258 --> 00:12:05.802
Celia, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:12:05.802 --> 00:12:07.642
Your One Word, and for taking that picture

00:12:07.642 --> 00:12:09.473
and tweeting it out as well.

00:12:09.473 --> 00:12:11.058
I really, really, really appreciate it

00:12:11.058 --> 00:12:12.328
and I hope you're enjoying the book.

00:12:12.328 --> 00:12:14.119
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:14.119 --> 00:12:15.202
I believe in you.

00:12:15.202 --> 00:12:17.121
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:12:17.121 --> 00:12:19.093
and whatever your one word is.

00:12:19.093 --> 00:12:20.249
Much love.

00:12:20.249 --> 00:12:21.749
I'll see you soon.

00:12:27.417 --> 00:12:29.609
- I never really was the actress that said

00:12:29.609 --> 00:12:31.163
there was no work or la la,

00:12:31.163 --> 00:12:32.882
'cause I, look at my resume.

00:12:32.882 --> 00:12:34.952
I really can't complain.

00:12:34.952 --> 00:12:37.619
I've been in amazing, amazingly,

00:12:38.599 --> 00:12:40.324
I'm just an extreme optimist.

00:12:40.324 --> 00:12:41.405
That's how I was raised.

00:12:41.405 --> 00:12:42.912
I mean, I came from the hood.

00:12:42.912 --> 00:12:44.848
You can't be a pessimist
coming from the hood

00:12:44.848 --> 00:12:46.225
if you think you going to make it out.

00:12:46.225 --> 00:12:50.968
You know, so I just never
thought about how bad it was.

00:12:50.968 --> 00:12:53.158
I was thinking about how
can I make a difference?

00:12:53.158 --> 00:12:54.563
How can I make a change?

00:12:54.563 --> 00:12:55.680
And that's what I focused on.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:56.988
I never thought about, woe is me.

00:12:56.988 --> 00:12:57.821
It's so hard.

00:12:57.821 --> 00:12:58.816
No one gives me a job.

00:12:58.816 --> 00:12:59.706
You're going to give me a job.

00:12:59.706 --> 00:13:02.362
Let me in the room and
eventually you'll pay attention,

00:13:02.362 --> 00:13:04.805
and I think that's what
people are witnessing now.

00:13:04.805 --> 00:13:07.408
I've been doing this for a long time

00:13:07.408 --> 00:13:09.416
and I stayed in my lane.

00:13:09.416 --> 00:13:11.326
I never hated on anyone.

00:13:11.326 --> 00:13:13.783
I think there's room for all of us,

00:13:13.783 --> 00:13:15.487
and I think that's what
people are witnessing,

00:13:15.487 --> 00:13:18.005
of someone who waited, waited,

00:13:18.005 --> 00:13:19.106
waited their turn.

00:13:19.106 --> 00:13:20.852
(laughing)

